Content:
Couple of issues;

Firsrt of all most humans are not rational. Changing a habit is difficult, especially if the alternative is (momentarily) worse. 
Second of all NYC is infamous for taking big sums of money and doing... nothing. (I am not from NYC, but watch Louis Rossmann on that lol)

@WendoverProductions
To solve the elitism question has anyone tried tying the cost of entry to the value of the vehicle? 
Rich people drive nice cars, and if you are doing this via a digital Epass you can force them to tell you what type of car it is being used.  If they try to cheat the system all of the epass readers have cameras.
